course: dictionary
lesson: 1863
title: Coiled: wound into loops
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Coiled» means wound into rings or loops, one on top of another, like a rope or a spring. The context gives the clue: «Ammonites were sea animals with coiled shells.» A shell that is coiled winds round in rings, so coiled must mean wound round like that.
explain: «Coiled» can also be the past form of the verb «coil». It tells you that someone wound something into loops. Try the swap test: put «wound into loops» in place of «coiled» in «The hose was coiled on the reel». If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: «Coiled» can describe a body held tight and ready to move. «The lion lay coiled, ready to spring.» The clues are «ready to spring» and «lay still», so coiled here means tense and waiting. Stories often say a character «coiled like a spring».
fact: Coiled means wound into rings or circles, one on top of another.
fact: «Coiled» is also the past form of the verb «coil», as in «The rope was coiled neatly».
fact: «Coiled» can describe a body or muscle held tight and ready to move suddenly.
fact: «A crane's windpipe is very long and coiled inside its breastbone like a trumpet's tube.»
fact: Coiled springs and coiled wire are used in science, for example in a light bulb or an electromagnet.
exercise: «A snake lay coiled in the sun.» What does coiled mean here? | *Wound into loops, one on top of another | Very hot and sandy | Stretched out flat in a straight line | Dropped on the sand and broken
exercise: «A crane's windpipe is very long and coiled inside its breastbone like a trumpet's tube.» What is the windpipe compared to? | Lost in the woods | *A trumpet's tube | A loud, deep call | A crane's breastbone
exercise: «The cat coiled, tense and ready to pounce.» What does coiled suggest? | *Held tight, ready to move suddenly | Wound into a rope for the hook | Fast asleep and snoring | Sitting still for a photo
test: «Dad coiled the garden hose and hung it on the wall.» What did Dad do with the hose? | Filled it with water | *Wound it into loops | Cut it into pieces
test: Coiled is the past form of which verb? | Cool | *Coil | Crawl | Cover
exam: Which sentence uses coiled to mean ready to move suddenly? | *The lion lay coiled, ready to spring | The hose was coiled on the reel | The wire was coiled round the bulb | The rope lay coiled on the deck
